<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"/><title>Isaac cube · Campaign viewer</title><meta name="description" content="Filter 49,152 recorded Isaac cube trials and inspect eight-corner tilt percentile plots, mechanics, controller gains and delays."/><link rel="stylesheet" href="/isaac-viewer/style.css"/></head><body>
<header><a href="/en/">One-Piece / Engineering Agents</a><nav><a href="/isaac/">Isaac campaigns</a><a href="/isaac/report/">Full technical report</a><button id="mobile-filters" aria-controls="filters" aria-expanded="false">Show filters</button></nav></header>
<div class="shell"><aside id="filters" aria-label="Case filters"><h2>Select trials</h2><p class="caption">Choose recorded cases, then apply the filters.</p><form id="filter-form">
<label>Architecture<select id="campaign"><option value="reference">Reference · 166.2 mm</option><option value="candidate">Candidate · 180.0 mm</option><option value="both">Compare both</option></select></label>
<div class="label">Supported corners</div><div id="corners" class="corners"></div>
<label>Initial tilt preset<select id="preset"><option value="full">Full range · 0–5°</option><option value="small">Small release · 0–2°</option><option value="large">Larger release · 2–5°</option><option value="custom">Custom range</option></select></label>
<div class="label">Initial rotation radius (°)</div><div class="range"><label>Minimum<input id="radius-min" type="number" step="0.1" value="0"/></label><label>Maximum<input id="radius-max" type="number" step="0.1" value="5"/></label></div>
<div class="label">Initial yaw rate (rad/s)</div><div class="range"><label>Minimum<input id="yaw-min" type="number" step="0.05" value="-1"/></label><label>Maximum<input id="yaw-max" type="number" step="0.05" value="1"/></label></div>
<details><summary>Rotation direction and components</summary><div id="direction-filters"></div></details>
<details><summary>Mechanical properties</summary><p class="caption">Recorded values select a design. They do not change or rerun it.</p><div id="mechanical-filters"></div></details>
<details><summary>Gains, observation delay and noise</summary><div id="timing-filters"></div><p class="caption">Network latency, jitter and packet loss were not modeled. Exact gains are in Test setup.</p></details>
<details><summary>Outcomes, GPUs and exact cases</summary><label>Screening outcome<select id="outcome"><option value="all">All outcomes</option><option value="passed">Passed</option><option value="failed">Failed</option></select></label><label>Termination status<select id="termination"><option value="all">All statuses</option><option value="completed">Completed</option><option value="lost_balance">Lost balance</option><option value="lost_contact">Lost contact</option><option value="excessive_slip">Excessive slip</option><option value="numerical_failure">Numerical failure</option></select></label><label>GPU indices, comma-separated<input id="gpus" placeholder="Blank = all six GPUs"/></label><label>Exact noise seeds, comma-separated<input id="seeds"/></label><label>Exact case IDs, comma-separated<input id="case-ids"/></label></details>
<div class="button-row"><button type="submit" class="primary">Apply filters</button><button type="reset">Reset</button></div></form><button id="copy-link">Copy link to this selection</button><p class="caption">The full technical report describes the complete campaigns. It does not change with these filters.</p><a href="/isaac/report/" download="isaac-cube-technical-report.html">Download full report</a></aside>
<main><div class="eyebrow">Recorded simulation evidence · 24 October 2026</div><h1>Eight corners. Two cube designs.</h1><p class="lead">Follow the tilt over time and inspect exactly which initial conditions, mechanics and control settings produced it.</p><div id="error" class="note error" role="alert" hidden></div><div id="metrics" class="metrics"></div><p id="selection-caption" class="caption"></p><div id="status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Loading the recorded campaign catalog…</div>
<div class="tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Evidence views"><button role="tab" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="trajectories" id="tab-trajectories">Tilt trajectories</button><button role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="setup" id="tab-setup">Test setup</button><button role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="exports" id="tab-exports">Cases &amp; exports</button></div>
<section id="trajectories" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-trajectories"><h2>Tilt over time, corner by corner</h2><div class="toolbar"><label>Motion after stopping<select id="mode"><option value="all-recorded">Include all recorded motion</option><option value="evaluation-only">Through evaluation stop only</option></select></label><label>Tilt measurement<select id="metric"><option value="tilt_total_deg">Total tilt (°)</option><option value="tilt_x_deg">Tilt x (°)</option><option value="tilt_y_deg">Tilt y (°)</option></select></label><label>Vertical scale<select id="zoom"><option value="full">Full recorded range</option><option value="near">Near upright · 0–5°</option><option value="fine">Fine detail · 0–0.5°</option></select></label></div><label class="check"><input id="paths" type="checkbox"/>Draw every selected trajectory (downloads full-resolution tilt records)</label><div id="policy" class="note"></div><div class="legend"><span><i style="--swatch:#719fb2"></i>68.3%</span><span><i style="--swatch:#b0ccd6"></i>95.5%</span><span><i style="--swatch:#dce7eb"></i>99.7%</span><span><i style="--swatch:#eff3f3"></i>100%</span><span><i style="--swatch:#24566d"></i>Reference median</span><span><i style="--swatch:#b64628"></i>Candidate median</span></div><div id="charts" class="charts"></div><p class="caption">Pointwise central empirical coverage across all selected cases; no trajectory subsampling. These bands are not confidence intervals or Gaussian assumptions. Dashed lines mark the 5° peak screening limit and 20° stop threshold. Hover or touch a panel for values and contributing counts. Zoom can clip larger values; exported quantiles remain unchanged.</p></section>
<section id="setup" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-setup" hidden><h2>What was actually tested</h2><p>The same saved controller was used for both mechanical configurations and all eight corners. Sidebar filters select archived cases; they do not run new simulations.</p><h3>Mechanical configurations</h3><div id="mechanics-table" class="table-wrap"></div><h3>Timing, observations and communication</h3><div id="timing-table" class="table-wrap"></div><p class="caption">The 15 ms delay is a simulated observation delay, not a measured communication latency. Encoders and coordinate transformations use ideal simulator state. Plotted tilt is geometric truth, not the noisy feedback signal.</p><h3>Saved controller and exact gains</h3><div id="controllers"></div><h3>Initial conditions</h3><p>Each campaign has 24,576 cases, with 3,072 per corner. Initial rotation radius is uniform on [0,5]°, direction uniform on [−180,180]°, and world yaw rate uniform on [−1,1] rad/s. The paired plan and per-case noise seeds are identical between campaigns. Uniform radius gives greater density near upright than a uniform-area disk.</p><details><summary>Exact model inputs, screening gates and provenance</summary><pre id="exact-inputs"></pre></details></section>
<section id="exports" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-exports" hidden><h2>Reproduce this selection</h2><p>Comparison pass rates and quantiles keep the two architectures separate. Outcome filters describe a conditional subset.</p><div id="summary-table" class="table-wrap"></div><div class="button-row"><button id="download-csv" disabled>Percentile CSV</button><button id="download-receipt" disabled>Selection receipt JSON</button><button id="download-cases" disabled>All selected cases JSON</button></div><p class="caption">Case export downloads the matching metadata, including every selected case ID, seed, initial state, stop and recorded screening result. The full original telemetry archives remain separate.</p><pre id="filter-preview"></pre></section>
<footer>Existing numerical exploration, not physical acceptance. MuJoCo–PhysX agreement remains inconclusive. <a href="/isaac/report/">Read the complete protocol and limitations</a>. <a href="/isaac/publication.json">Publication provenance</a>. No GPU-server connection or SSH tunnel is required.</footer></main></div><script is:inline type="module" src="/isaac-viewer/app.mjs"></script></body></html>
